  33:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *\n
  34:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *<b>Description </b>\n
  35:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *The fsRam package provides the parts outlined in the model. By compilation switch, the Ram task m
  36:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *the usual operating mode or in test harness mode. When running in the usual operating mode, the t
  37:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *will not be linked to the package. When running in test harness mode, stub services are provided,
  38:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *RAM checking interface is separated from being called and only the test server will be able to ca
  39:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *\n
  40:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *<b>Rationale </b>\n
  41:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *At normal operational work, checking the whole RAM at once is not possible, at least a very diffi
  42:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *reason, it was decided to perform a full RAM check at startup only. Below an overview is provided
  43:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *is used comparable to some other public algorithms. Fault models can be found at the respective i
  44:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *\n
  45:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *\image html RAM_Test_Algorithm.jpg
  46:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *\n
  47:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *As shown the quality of the implemented algorithm is comparable to the March Y algorithm extended
  48:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *the March-LR algorithm. The comparison table shows the implemented algorithm to be able to cover 
  49:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *data cells and address lines as well. The RAM check task is implemented using assembler language 
  50:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *C-wrapper function on its top, thus it depends on the type of controller.
  51:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *\n
  52:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *During normal operational work, the March-X algorithm is used to continue checking the RAM. As th
  53:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *\n
  54:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRam.c ****  *\n
